/**

\page page_third-party_hdf5 HDF5 and NetCDF

\tableofcontents


## HDF5

Peano does not need HDF5. There's no generic input file format, and it can write
its own mesh files without HDF5. Things are different if you want to dump HDF5,
or if you use an extension which requires HDF5. HDF5 support is controlled
by the CMake option PEANO_WITH_HDF5, which is enabled by default:

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
cmake .. -DPEANO_WITH_HDF5=ON
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

You do not have to specify any paths or libraries manually. CMake locates HDF5 via
find_package(HDF5 COMPONENTS C) and links the resulting HDF5::HDF5 target, so the
correct include directories and libraries are picked up automatically. If your HDF5
installation lives in a non-standard location, point CMake at it through the usual
HDF5_ROOT environment variable or CMake hint.

Only the C component of HDF5 is required; Peano does not use the HDF5 C++ binding.
If PEANO_WITH_HDF5 is on but no HDF5 installation can be found, the build emits a
warning and continues with HDF5 support disabled. The HDF5 installation must
support parallel I/O.


## NetCDF

NetCDF might be required by some applications. As with HDF5, support is enabled
through a CMake option, PEANO_WITH_NETCDF, which is on by default:

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
cmake .. -DPEANO_WITH_NETCDF=ON
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

NetCDF is located by cmake/FindNetCDF.cmake. This helper queries pkg-config (when
available) and also honours a number of environment hints, so in most cases no
further configuration is needed. If NetCDF lives in a non-standard location, point
the build at it via one of the following environment variables before invoking
CMake:

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
export NETCDF_DIR=/path/to/netcdf            # prefix containing include/ and lib/
# or, more specifically:
export NETCDF_INCLUDE_DIR=/path/to/netcdf/include
export NETCDF_LIB_DIR=/path/to/netcdf/lib
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

If PEANO_WITH_NETCDF is on but no NetCDF installation can be found, the build emits
a warning and continues with NetCDF support disabled. The NetCDF installation must
provide NetCDF-4 (HDF5 backend) support and parallel I/O.


*/
